extends RefCounted

# ============================================================
#   ALL THE LEVELS
#
#   32 levels, like the first Super Mario: 8 worlds with 4 levels
#   each, in 4 AREAS. Every area ends in a castle with a boss:
#
#      AREA 1  ends at 2-4, the POODLE's castle
#      AREA 2  ends at 4-4, the GOLDEN RETRIEVER's castle
#      AREA 3  ends at 6-4, the HUSKY's ice castle
#      AREA 4  ends at 8-4, the DOG HOUSE, with the big Doggie
#
#   Every letter below is one square of the world.
#   Change the letters, press play, and your level changes.
#
#      .  sky (nothing)        C  a coin
#      G  ground (grass, sand or snow on top — the look decides)
#      D  dirt                 B  a wooden box
#      S  where the cat starts
#      F  a checkpoint flag    W  the sandwich (finish!)
#      T  a tree (a cactus in the desert, a mushroom in a cave)
#      b  a bush (a snowman in the snow!)
#      H  a dog house          X  the boss            A  the axe
#
#      ^  spikes — they hurt          ~  water — you swim in it
#      =  a ladder — press UP         k  a key
#      L  a locked door (needs a key)
#      E  a bat — it flies in a wavy line, you CAN stomp it
#      M  a mushroom baddie — stomp it!
#      O  a spiky ball — rolls at you, you CANNOT stomp it
#
#      p  a pipe — stack them up to make it taller
#      _  a ledge — jump up through it from underneath
#      m  a mushroom top — jump up through it too
#      |  a mushroom stalk (just for looks)
#      >  an arrow sign (just for looks)
#      f  a fence (just for looks)
#
#   And the blocks. Bonk them from underneath with your head and
#   something comes out:
#
#      !  LUCKY BLOCK  →  a surprise! Could be coins, coffee, a
#                          nugget suit, a heart, a chip, a diamond...
#                          or a mushroom baddie, if you're unlucky.
#      ?  ORANGE block →  a CHICKEN NUGGET suit
#      R  RED block    →  a heart, to get a lost one back
#      N  GREEN block  →  a CHIP — run much faster for ten seconds
#      U  BLUE block   →  a diamond — nothing can hurt you
#      Y  BROWN block  →  a cup of coffee, for fire powers
#
#   Every level needs a "name" (like "2-3"), a "title" (the words
#   on screen when it starts), a "look" (see LOOKS in
#   cat_world.gd) and its "rows". The first level of an area also
#   has an "area", and a castle has a "boss" — "poodle", "golden",
#   "husky" or "dog" (see BOSSES in dog.gd).
#
#   Every level has 14 rows, so it fits the screen exactly. The
#   rows can be as long as you like.
#
#   Want a level 33? Copy a whole level, from its { to its },
#   paste it before the last one, and give it a new name.
#   To play just one level, start the game with  -- --level=2-3
# ============================================================

